  "summary": "Mary Magdalene is a follower of Jesus named in all the Gospels. Luke says she was freed of seven demons, and the Gospels place her at the crucifixion and empty tomb; John makes her the first to see the risen Jesus. The later image of her as a repentant prostitute comes from a 591 sermon, not the Gospels.",
